<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Acer Jan-Sept net down 36.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Acer Jan-Sept net down 36.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-September 1996</p>
<p>			 (in million T$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Turnover			    42,114 vs 40,046</p>
<p>    Net profit			   2,221 vs  3,493</p>
<p>NOTE - Acer Inc is Taiwan's largest computer firm.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that it expected sales to improve because the fourth quarter is the traditional hot sales season for electronic firms and because prices of dynamic random access memory have stabilised.</p>
<p>The company has lowered its 1996 profit target to T$3.0 billion on sales of T$68.52 billion, compared with an earlier target of T$6.0 billion on sales of T$80 billion.</p>
<p>It attributed the lower 1996 profit and sales targets to falling semiconductor prices and poor performance in the global personal computer market.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (-5080815)</p>
</text>
